On September 18, 2026, President Trump announced that CNN, MS NOW, and Politico were banned from the White House (see: https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/117293599348325006).

This market will resolve to "Yes" if Donald Trump or the White House publicly and officially announce that any additional news outlets are banned from the White House between market creation and the specified date, 11:59 PM ET. Otherwise, this market will resolve to “No.”

A qualifying announcement must name one or more outlets additional to CNN, MS NOW, & Politico, by name.

The following do not qualify as official announcements:
- Anonymous, unattributed, or leaked statements not confirmed as official;
- Statements by persons not authorized to speak for the parties listed above;
- Third-party speculation, analysis, or reporting that a ban will be announced;
- Satirical, fabricated, hacked, or impersonated communications;
- Statements that a ban is prospective, contingent, or conditional rather than announcing a present, decided ban — for example that other outlets "may," or "could" be banned, or a threat to ban outlets absent some other outcome.

Once a qualifying announcement is made, this market will resolve to "Yes" regardless of whether the ban is later reversed or rescinded, or is ever actually enforced.

The primary resolution source for this market will be official information from Donald Trump and The White House.

